# Supabase CLI scratch
supabase/.temp/

# Customer PO / intake spreadsheets get dropped in the working tree.
# They are real order data and must never be committed.
*.xlsx
*.xls

# Reference photos for the slip-printing work: sample box/roll slips carry real
# party names, PO numbers and quantities. Same rule as the spreadsheets above —
# the folder structure and its README stay tracked, the images never do.
docs/printing-reference/**
!docs/printing-reference/README.md
!docs/printing-reference/*/
!docs/printing-reference/*/.gitkeep
# Narrow exception: the two BarTender canvas shots the compact roll slips were
# built from. They are blank templates — <Empty> in every data field, no party,
# no PO, no quantity — so the reason this folder is ignored does not reach them,
# and RollSlipCompactLabel.tsx is meaningless without the layout it copies.
!docs/printing-reference/02-bartender/template-roll-slip-small-new-4x6.jpeg
!docs/printing-reference/02-bartender/template-roll-small-slip-2x3.jpeg

# macOS Finder metadata — never belongs in the repo.
.DS_Store

# Working reference shots kept at the repo root. Both carry third-party data —
# a consignment address slip with a customer's postal address, and a Job
# Separation screenshot showing a live PO number, quantity and unit rate — and
# one of this repo's remotes is public. Same rule as docs/printing-reference/:
# useful on disk, never in a commit.
/Address slip.jpeg
/Job Sep.jpeg

# Hollow copy of the shade card tracker, kept on disk only. It carries no
# source code — the real project lives at mrpal5a/novelty-shade-card-tracker —
# but it does hold a .env.local with live Supabase credentials, and one of
# this repo's remotes is public. Never commit it.
/SHADECARD/
